# Patch:        060-field-default-shims
# Phase:        pre
# Target:       binary-field/src/aes/packed.rs, binary-field/src/bitslice/packing.rs, binary-field/src/field_defaults.rs, binary-field/src/lib.rs
# Hunks:        4
# Class:        equiv-rewrite
# Gap:          docs/extractor-issues.md 9: a call to a default method of
#               p3-field's traits takes the type's whole `Field` dictionary,
#               which reaches the mutually recursive trait group; for a field's
#               `Div` impl, which calls `Field::inverse`, the `Field` impl and
#               the `Div` impl are themselves mutually recursive. Without this
#               patch aeneas stops: "Mixed declaration groups (which contain
#               both type and function declarations or functions and traits,
#               for instance) are not supported yet".
# Cost:         none in a normal build: the copies are compiled but unused
#               there. In the extracted variant, inherent `inverse`, `is_zero`
#               and `is_one` shadow the `Field` defaults at every call site on
#               a concrete field type of this crate, and call copies of the
#               default bodies.
# Upstreamable: no: the shims exist only for the extractor.
# Drop when:    aeneas accepts p3-field's trait hierarchy (issue 9).
# Test:         test p3-binary-field --lib pre_patch_060
# Mutation:     `raw_is_zero` compares with `ONE`, so it disagrees with
#               `Field::is_zero` and the differential test fails.
#
# `Field::inverse`, `is_zero` and `is_one` have default bodies
# (`self.try_inverse().expect("Tried to invert zero")`, `*self == Self::ZERO`,
# `*self == Self::ONE`), and no type here overrides them. Called on a concrete
# type, each still takes the type's `Field` dictionary. That pulls in the whole
# impl and, through it, `Gf2`'s (every type's `PrimeSubfield`), the serde
# supertraits, and the trait group aeneas rejects. `impl_div_methods!`'s `Div`
# calls `inverse`, so a field's `Div` impl and its `Field` impl become mutually
# recursive, which aeneas rejects outright.
#
# `field_defaults.rs` gives each of the twelve field types copies of the three
# default bodies (`raw_*`, compiled in every build) and, under
# cfg(hax_backend_lean), inherent methods of the trait methods' names that call
# them. Method resolution prefers inherent methods, so the call sites, the
# `Div` impls `impl_div_methods!` expands here included, reach the copies
# without being edited. Two files then no longer use their `Field` import
# under the cfg, which is allowed there.
#
# The differential test compares each copy with the trait default on zero, one,
# the generator and 64 random elements of each type, and checks that
# `raw_inverse` panics on zero.
#
